{
  "_note": "How effects look (docs/07-cinematics-and-vfx.md, the build decision in docs/11-milestones.md). `looks` has one entry per element: colours, particles, light (a `flicker` jitters it) and sound. Colours above 1 glow. Particle kinds: 0 soft glow, 1 shard, 2 streak, 3 smoke, 4 spark, 5 leaf, 6 mist, and pixel glyphs 7 note, 8 two notes, 9 lantern. `moves` says which delivery and look each skill, ward or creature move uses; `pose` is the anim to play (a hero's by its Eldwin name, wiz_side_<motion>, played from their own sheet, or as their cast until it is drawn), `release` the anim frame the effect leaves on. The `song` delivery sends notes off the instrument to each target, and its `song` says which kind: finale (more, bigger, brighter notes for each Verse spent, which the battle passes on the effect as `scale`, 1 to 5), turn (the notes change colour in flight to the element the battle passes as `element`), ring (one short song per target, in the elements passed as `elements`, in target order, else round the six), lullaby (slow notes over every foe while the light dims a little). A defend whose line has delivery `ward` takes its look and stance from it. Anything not listed falls back on its target and element, so a new skill needs only a new line, and a new element only a new look (decision 0376). A move's `sound` plays on top of its look's, `soundAt` seconds in (the Pale Hart's hooves, Applejack's hiccup).",
